, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Adverbs of Manner", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is done. <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">She strongly voiced her concerns. How did she voice her concerns? Strongly.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ly</span> to an adjective: <br> Examples: routine \u2192 routinely             quick \u2192 quickly", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ally</span><br> Example:  public \u2192  publicly", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These adverbs can come after the direct object or after the verb if there isn't any direct object.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Habits and Routines", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about someone's habits and routines, you use the Present Simple tense and frequency words.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use expressions of frequency to say how many times you do an activity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This can be an adverb like <span class=\"italic\">often</span>, <span class=\"italic\">sometimes</span> or <span class=\"italic\">never</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It can also be an expression like <span class=\"italic\">a lot</span>, <span class=\"italic\">all the time</span> or<span class=\"italic\"> when I can</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Expressions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"always<br> usually<br> often<br> sometimes<br> occasionally<br> hardly ever<br> never\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"every day/week/month<br> most of the time<br> every other day/week/month<br> once in a while<br> from time to time<br> when ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Perry usually walks in the park. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Carol always gives good advice.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to guarantee ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to promise that something is true or real  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guarantee you Doug, this time it will work out!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about people's routines.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to thrive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to grow or develop successfully ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I thrive on the excitement.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "routinely", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a regular way of doing things in a particular order ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I routinely do meditation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get rid of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to no longer have, want, or need something or someone ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I just need to get rid of any fears.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "undoubtedly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "definitely true or existing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Undoubtedly, this will be one of your best nights ever!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "frequently", "type": "name"}, {"content": "happens often ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I frequently sit in the park or read a book.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10aud05-2", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take a walk ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to walk without a purpose ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I frequently take a walk to relax. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le07ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Role play a situation. Talk about your plans for going out on a blind date.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your partner will play the role of your friend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the Present Continuous tense to talk about plans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use adverbs of manner to describe how things happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I do a role play.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about future plans.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe how things happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I change roles.", "type": "text"}]}]}